WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:03.269
-A whistle-blower
has reportedly claimed

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:05.371
that President Trump
made a troubling promise

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:06.572
to a foreign leader.

00:00:06.572 --> 00:00:08.975
for more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:13.312
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.312 --> 00:00:15.248
-Yesterday the President
flew to San Diego

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:18.818
to visit a section of his dumb
border wall which was reportedly

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:21.187
just a replacement
reinforcement barrier

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:24.590
erected in an area where smaller
barriers had already existed.

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:26.859
And, as usual,
Trump was impressed

00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:28.494
with the stupidest details

00:00:28.494 --> 00:00:31.764
like the fact that the wall
was supposedly super hot.

00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:35.368
-It's designed to absorb heat,
so it's extremely hot.

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:37.537
The wall is --
you won't be able to touch it.

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:40.640
You can -- You can
fry an egg on that wall.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.508
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:42.508 --> 00:00:45.512
-You can fry an egg
on a wall?

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:46.846
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:48.881
I know there are a lot of things
he doesn't understand,

00:00:48.881 --> 00:00:52.084
but I didn't think
gravity was on that list.

00:00:52.084 --> 00:00:53.085
Did he see --

00:00:53.085 --> 00:00:57.123
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:59.559
Do you think he saw
a Salvador Dalí painting

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:01.127
and think it was a cookbook?

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:03.295 line:78%
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:03.295
"You can fry an egg
on that wall,

00:01:03.295 --> 00:01:05.698
and you can melt a clock
on that tree."

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:08.267
[laughter and applause]

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:09.468
I know the expression,

00:01:09.468 --> 00:01:11.137
"So hot you can
fry an egg on it,"

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:13.339
but I've never heard it
said about a wall.

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:15.208
Everything with this guy
is an infomercial.

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:16.709
"You heard of a frying pan.

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:19.245
Well, now we're introducing
the frying wall."

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:22.949
[laughter and applause]

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:26.986
Trump also tried to tout what
he claimed was new technology

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:28.187
that would allow the government

00:01:28.187 --> 00:01:30.022
to track people
trying to cross the border,

00:01:30.022 --> 00:01:32.491
but an official who was with him
on the trip

00:01:32.491 --> 00:01:34.994
tried to warn him against
saying anything about it.

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:36.929
-One thing we haven't
mentioned is technology.

00:01:36.929 --> 00:01:38.464
They're wired
so that we will know

00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:40.099
if somebody's trying
to break through

00:01:40.099 --> 00:01:42.368
and you may want to discuss
that a little bit, General.

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:45.205
-Sir, there could be some
merit in not discussing that.

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:46.205
-Okay.

00:01:46.205 --> 00:01:47.407
[ Laughter ]
I like that.

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:50.009
That was a great answer.
-Yeah.

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:51.544
-I'll just tell you
they're wired.

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:52.845
-My God.

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:55.047
This guy is supposed to be
the Commander in Chief.

00:01:55.047 --> 00:01:58.718
Could you imagine his fireside
chats during World War II?

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:01.721
"We'll be launching a top-secret
offensive against the Germans

00:02:01.721 --> 00:02:03.189
in an undisclosed location.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:05.825
General Eisenhower,
do you want to tell everyone

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:07.126
more about Normandy?

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:09.329
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:13.700
You're shaking your head no.

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:17.569
You were saying
it was a beach in France.

00:02:17.569 --> 00:02:20.473
Is that right?"

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:21.941
Now, Trump has gone to extreme

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:24.577
and possibly even illegal
lengths to get this wall.

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:27.346
For one thing, he's moved
hundreds of millions of dollars

00:02:27.346 --> 00:02:30.550
from programs like FEMA,
military schools, and daycare

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:33.052
to pay for border enforcement
and construction of the wall.

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:35.088
And on top of that,
he's so desperate

00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:37.490
to get the wall done
before the 2020 election,

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:39.492
he's actually promised pardons

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:42.661
to officials who have to break
the law to get it done.

00:02:42.661 --> 00:02:45.965
-President Trump promised
his supporters a border wall

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:48.567
and he plans to give it
to them by 2020.

00:02:48.567 --> 00:02:49.769
According to
the "Washington Post,"

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:51.471
the President
has directed aides

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:54.073
to fast track
billions of dollars worth

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:55.742
of construction contracts,

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:57.743
aggressively seize private land,

00:02:57.743 --> 00:03:00.479
and disregard
environmental rules.

00:03:00.479 --> 00:03:01.880
And according
to the reporting --

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:03.616
this is coming right
out of the "Washington Post" --

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:05.852
he also told
worried subordinates

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:09.221
that he will pardon them
of any potential wrongdoing

00:03:09.221 --> 00:03:10.923
should they have to break laws

00:03:10.923 --> 00:03:13.026
to get the barriers
built quickly.

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:14.894
-He promised to pardon them.

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:16.996
But, of course, the unspoken
promise

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:19.965
is he will forget
he ever said that.

00:03:19.965 --> 00:03:22.001
"Hey, I did what you said.
Can I get that pardon?"

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:23.436
"I'd love to help you,
I'm very busy.

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:26.572
I'm trying to get this God damn
egg to stick to the wall."

00:03:26.572 --> 00:03:28.741
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:30.743
Trump is openly
flouting the law

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:32.578
by dangling pardons
for illegal behavior,

00:03:32.578 --> 00:03:34.147
and, of course,
this isn't the first time

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:36.549
he's just openly defied
legal requirements

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:38.184
like subpoenas from Congress.

00:03:38.184 --> 00:03:39.752
In fact, at this very moment,

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:41.954
his administration
is refusing to give Congress

00:03:41.954 --> 00:03:43.489
a secret whistle-blower
complaint

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:44.857
from within
the intelligence community.

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:47.693
Now, we don't know exactly
what's in the complaint,

00:03:47.693 --> 00:03:49.128
but last night,
the "Washington Post"

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:50.697
reported something stunning.

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:52.932
It has to do with
the President himself

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:56.201
making a reportedly troubling
promise to a foreign leader.

00:03:56.201 --> 00:03:58.871
-The story that is rocking
Washington this morning.

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:00.640
A communication between
President Trump

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:03.409
and a foreign leader prompting
a whistle-blower complaint.

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:06.679
-Former US intelligence official
familiar with the matter

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:09.414
told NBC News President Trump
spoke by phone

00:04:09.414 --> 00:04:12.352
to a world leader over
the summer and made a promise.

00:04:12.352 --> 00:04:14.887
We do not know
what the promise was.

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:17.990
We do not know
who the foreign leader is.

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:20.927
-President Trump's interaction
with the foreign leader

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:24.430
included a promise that
was regarded was so troubling

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:27.466
that it prompted an official
in the US intelligence community

00:04:27.466 --> 00:04:29.636
to file a formal
whistle-blower complaint

00:04:29.636 --> 00:04:32.738
with the inspector general
for the intelligence community.

00:04:32.738 --> 00:04:33.939
-That's right.

00:04:33.939 --> 00:04:35.908
Trump reportedly promised
something so troubling

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:38.844
an intelligence official filed
a whistle-blower complaint.

00:04:38.844 --> 00:04:41.480
Now, we don't know which foreign
leader this is,

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:43.015
and this is a
complicated story.

00:04:43.015 --> 00:04:44.416
so just to help you
follow along,

00:04:44.416 --> 00:04:46.819
we put together a helpful
little mnemonic device.

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:50.123
Remember, it's a promise
from the United States,

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:53.692
made by Trump to an
international leader,

00:04:53.692 --> 00:04:56.629
but we do not know
their name.

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:57.663
Could be anyone.

00:04:57.663 --> 00:05:00.833
[ Laughter and applause ]
Could be anyone.

00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:05.171
And I -- I for one
am just shocked

00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:08.140
this is the first whistle-blower
complaint Trump has had.

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:09.508
The way this guy behaves,

00:05:09.508 --> 00:05:11.710
there should be literal
whistle-blowers

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:13.646
following him
everywhere he goes.

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:14.914
-We're dealing
with a Democrat--

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:18.584
[ Whistles blaring ]

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:20.553
-Now today,
Trump responded to this report,

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:22.955
not by insisting he would
never do such a thing,

00:05:22.955 --> 00:05:25.858
but claiming that he was
too smart to do such a thing.

00:05:25.858 --> 00:05:27.292
Here's the first part
of his tweet.

00:05:27.292 --> 00:05:29.595
"Another fake news story
out there, it never ends."

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:32.130
Virtually, any time I speak on
the phone to a foreign leader,

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:34.433
I understand that there
may be many people listening

00:05:34.433 --> 00:05:35.968
from various US agencies.

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:39.071
Not to mention those
from the other country, itself.

00:05:39.071 --> 00:05:40.672
No problem."

00:05:40.672 --> 00:05:43.476
Why does he end his tweet like
we asked him for a favor?

00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:44.911
[ Laughter ]

00:05:44.911 --> 00:05:47.013
"Hey, Donald, can you hop on
this car with a foreign leader

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:48.548
and also drop us off
at the airport?"

00:05:48.548 --> 00:05:51.150
"No problem, what terminal?"

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:53.352
Trump then continued in his
second tweet writing,

00:05:53.352 --> 00:05:54.987
"Is anybody dumb enough
to believe

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:56.521
that I would say something
inappropriate

00:05:56.521 --> 00:05:57.790
with a foreign leader

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:00.092
while on such a potentially
heavily-populated call?"

00:06:00.092 --> 00:06:02.528
It's not the we're dumb enough
to believe it.

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:04.430
It's that we're smart enough
to believe

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:05.831
you're dumb enough to do it.

00:06:05.831 --> 00:06:07.132
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:07.132 --> 00:06:12.137
So Trump is dangling pardons
for illegal behavior.

00:06:12.137 --> 00:06:14.640
He's making shocking promises
to foreign leaders.

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:17.843
He probably feels like he has
impunity to do whatever he wants

00:06:17.843 --> 00:06:20.380
because so far he's faced
almost no consequences.

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:22.348
I mean, remember the Mueller
report?

00:06:22.348 --> 00:06:24.517
It was full of incredibly
damning evidence

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:26.318
about the President
welcoming and encouraging

00:06:26.318 --> 00:06:27.720
the help of a foreign
government,

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.589
his financial ties
to that government,

00:06:29.589 --> 00:06:31.924
and his attempts
to obstruct the investigation.

00:06:31.924 --> 00:06:33.258
That report came out in April,

00:06:33.258 --> 00:06:35.428
more than five months ago,
and in the meantime,

00:06:35.428 --> 00:06:37.163
Democratic leaders
have been arguing

00:06:37.163 --> 00:06:39.064
over whether to move forward
with impeachment.

00:06:39.064 --> 00:06:40.799
In fact, they can't even
seem to agree

00:06:40.799 --> 00:06:42.902
on the words they should use.

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:45.371
-The House Judiciary Committee
just this morning

00:06:45.371 --> 00:06:48.607
approved new ground rules
for its impeachment inquiry

00:06:48.607 --> 00:06:51.310
or investigation or both.

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:55.281
-Some call this process
an impeachment inquiry.

00:06:55.281 --> 00:06:58.184
Some call it
an impeachment investigation.

00:06:58.184 --> 00:07:00.686
There's no legal difference
between these terms,

00:07:00.686 --> 00:07:03.722
and I no longer care
to argue about nomenclature.

00:07:03.722 --> 00:07:05.491
-But it seems
other House Leaders

00:07:05.491 --> 00:07:07.993
do still care
about the nomenclature,

00:07:07.993 --> 00:07:10.896
with the House Speaker
still refusing to say

00:07:10.896 --> 00:07:13.232
that the House has launched
such an investigation.

00:07:13.232 --> 00:07:15.000
-Is the specific language
not important?

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:17.002
I mean, how should the American
people understand the work...

00:07:17.002 --> 00:07:18.403
-The American people
will understand --

00:07:18.403 --> 00:07:19.705
-...when members are speaking
very differently about it.

00:07:19.705 --> 00:07:22.107
-Impeachment is a very
divisive measure,

00:07:22.107 --> 00:07:25.077
but if we have to go there,
we'll have to go there.

00:07:25.077 --> 00:07:27.546
But we can't go there
unless we have the facts.

00:07:27.546 --> 00:07:29.615
-What do you mean unless
you have the facts?

00:07:29.615 --> 00:07:30.816
you have the facts.

00:07:30.816 --> 00:07:33.686
Robert Mueller wrote
a 448-page report,

00:07:33.686 --> 00:07:35.621
and I assure you,
there are lots of facts in it.

00:07:35.621 --> 00:07:38.824
Robert Mueller can't write a
text message to his wife

00:07:38.824 --> 00:07:40.326
without facts in it.

00:07:40.326 --> 00:07:42.027
"Should be home in half an hour.

00:07:42.027 --> 00:07:44.296
Pursuant to all applicable
Federal Regulations

00:07:44.296 --> 00:07:46.265
governing the operation
of automobiles

00:07:46.265 --> 00:07:48.301
under jurisdiction
of Federal Code 23-C,

00:07:48.301 --> 00:07:51.103
subsection 19
regarding speed limits

00:07:51.103 --> 00:07:54.139
and the use of signaling devices
to conduct lane changes

00:07:54.139 --> 00:07:56.909
and assuming the availability
of premium-grade fuel

00:07:56.909 --> 00:07:58.777
that meets or supersedes

00:07:58.777 --> 00:08:01.513
all relevant State and Federal
Efficiency standards,

00:08:01.513 --> 00:08:03.014
smiley face, heart emoji."

00:08:03.014 --> 00:08:04.116
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:04.116 --> 00:08:08.120
In fact, House Speaker --

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:11.090
House Speaker Nancy Pelosi
has apparently been so resistant

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:14.226
to attempts by other Democrats
to move forward with impeachment

00:08:14.226 --> 00:08:16.628
in the Judiciary Committee
led by Jerry Nadler

00:08:16.628 --> 00:08:19.298
that she slammed them
in a private meeting last week

00:08:19.298 --> 00:08:20.866
and then specifically told them

00:08:20.866 --> 00:08:23.268
to leak that private meeting
to the press.

00:08:23.268 --> 00:08:25.771
-House Speaker Nancy Pelosi
sending a loud message

00:08:25.771 --> 00:08:28.106
to her Judiciary Committee
chairman.

00:08:28.106 --> 00:08:29.842
Pull back on impeachment.

00:08:29.842 --> 00:08:32.577
"You can feel free
to leak this."

00:08:32.577 --> 00:08:35.681
That's what Pelosi told
lawmakers in a meeting last week

00:08:35.681 --> 00:08:38.050
according to multiple people
who spoke to POLITICO.

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:41.253
"This" refers to the Speaker's
displeasure at Jerry Nadler

00:08:41.253 --> 00:08:42.855
and his Judiciary Committee
staff.

00:08:42.855 --> 00:08:45.824
In that meeting, Pelosi
complained Nadler and his staff

00:08:45.824 --> 00:08:47.359
keep talking about impeachment

00:08:47.359 --> 00:08:49.729
as the likely result
of their investigations,

00:08:49.729 --> 00:08:54.233
which she sees as putting the
party at risk for a 2020 defeat.

00:08:54.233 --> 00:08:55.401
-Damn, she actually told them,

00:08:55.401 --> 00:08:57.369
"You can feel free
to leak this."

00:08:57.369 --> 00:08:59.872
it's like if your teacher caught
you passing notes in class

00:08:59.872 --> 00:09:01.840
and said, "do you mind
if I read this out loud?"

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:04.076
and you said, "Sure,"
and the note said, "You suck.

00:09:04.076 --> 00:09:05.544
Thanks for reading this
out loud."

00:09:05.544 --> 00:09:07.146
[ Laughter ]

00:09:07.146 --> 00:09:09.648
And yet, in spite of Pelosi's
reluctance, on Tuesday,

00:09:09.648 --> 00:09:12.285
we got even more damning
evidence of Trump's lawlessness

00:09:12.285 --> 00:09:13.518
when House Democrats grilled

00:09:13.518 --> 00:09:15.721
his former campaign manager,
Corey Lewandowski.

00:09:15.721 --> 00:09:18.423
Now, Tuesday's hearing was
weird to say the least

00:09:18.423 --> 00:09:20.459
because Lewandowski
is a prolific liar.

00:09:20.459 --> 00:09:21.727
When it comes to lying,

00:09:21.727 --> 00:09:24.430
Lewandowski even gives
Trump a run for his money.

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:26.765
When these two talk,
it must be Lie-A-Palooza.

00:09:26.765 --> 00:09:28.467
"Looking trim, Mr. President."

00:09:28.467 --> 00:09:29.869
"Thank you, Corey,
and may I say,

00:09:29.869 --> 00:09:31.637
you don't look anything
like a psychopath.

00:09:31.637 --> 00:09:33.205
[ Laughter ]

00:09:33.205 --> 00:09:37.342
Definitely don't look like
you're gonna do deck somebody."

00:09:37.342 --> 00:09:38.710
And on top of that,
Trump's White House

00:09:38.710 --> 00:09:41.213
invoked executive privilege
over his communications

00:09:41.213 --> 00:09:42.982
with Lewandowski,
which is insane,

00:09:42.982 --> 00:09:45.050
because Lewandowski
never worked in the White House,

00:09:45.050 --> 00:09:46.452
let alone the Executive Branch,

00:09:46.452 --> 00:09:49.121
and yet Lewandowski
insisted on stonewalling,

00:09:49.121 --> 00:09:51.590
which resulted
in exchanges like these.

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:54.226
-Did you ever suggest
to the President or anyone else

00:09:54.226 --> 00:09:56.062
that you thought your
communications with him

00:09:56.062 --> 00:09:58.698
were official
White House communications?

00:09:58.698 --> 00:10:00.032
-Congressman,
the White House has directed

00:10:00.032 --> 00:10:01.667
I not disclose the substance

00:10:01.667 --> 00:10:04.036
of any discussions with
the President or his advisers

00:10:04.036 --> 00:10:06.205
to protect Executive Branch
confidentiality.

00:10:06.205 --> 00:10:07.873
-How many times
has the President asked you

00:10:07.873 --> 00:10:11.410
to meet him in the White House?

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:12.911
-The White House has directed
I not disclose

00:10:12.911 --> 00:10:15.481
the substance of any--
-How many times did he direct

00:10:15.481 --> 00:10:18.016
you to deliver a message
to a member of his cabinet?

00:10:18.016 --> 00:10:19.819
-The White House has directed
I not disclose

00:10:19.819 --> 00:10:21.687
the substance of any discussions
with the President.

00:10:21.687 --> 00:10:23.855
-Did he ever discuss with you
any concerns

00:10:23.855 --> 00:10:25.925
that he may have committed
a criminal offense?

00:10:25.925 --> 00:10:28.360
-The White House has directed
I not disclose the substance

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:30.695
of any discussions with
the President or his advisers.

00:10:30.695 --> 00:10:34.032
-Has the president ever
offered you a pardon?

00:10:34.032 --> 00:10:36.102
-Again, the White House
has directed I not disclose

00:10:36.102 --> 00:10:37.369
the substance of any discussions

00:10:37.369 --> 00:10:38.770
with the President
or his advisers

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:41.073
to protect Executive Branch
confidentiality.

00:10:41.073 --> 00:10:44.777
-Wow, he won't say whether
Trump offered him a pardon not.

00:10:44.777 --> 00:10:47.480
Man, his seat is so hot,
you could fry an egg on it.

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:48.781
[ Laughter ]

00:10:48.781 --> 00:10:50.415
I mean, once you turned it
sideways.

00:10:50.415 --> 00:10:53.218
Now, whether it's withholding
whistle-blower complaints

00:10:53.218 --> 00:10:55.688
from Congress or dangling
pardons to cover up crimes,

00:10:55.688 --> 00:10:57.856
Trump is a lawless President
acting like a guy

00:10:57.856 --> 00:10:59.491
who thinks he can get away
with whatever he wants.

00:10:59.491 --> 00:11:01.192
There's at least one way
to show him he's wrong,

00:11:01.192 --> 00:11:03.796
and that's impeachment,
but some Democratic leaders

00:11:03.796 --> 00:11:05.630
are afraid to even touch the
subject

00:11:05.630 --> 00:11:06.731
because they think it's...

00:11:06.731 --> 00:11:08.300
-Extremely hot.

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:09.902
-This has been "A Closer Look."

